    "lesson": {
      "title": "Why does × 10 change a decimal so much?",
      "instruction": "Multiply 12.34 by ten. Where does each block go?",
      "explanation": "Each column is worth ten times the one to its right. Multiplying by ten moves every block one column left past a fixed decimal point; trading one tenth for ten hundredths keeps the number the same."
